    "recording": {
      "description": "Cost of recording one change. Every pair applies the same operation to a store without the feature and to a store with it, back to back, and alternates which one goes first. The overhead of a pair is the difference of the two durations: synchronous is the time of the patchState call, total also includes the microtask that computes the patches. Pairs from all rounds are pooled and the median and mean are reported. The two stores are timed in the same loop because two separate timing runs differ by more than the effect (the plain operation takes milliseconds and varies with garbage collection).",
      "notes": [
        "The timeline store is cleared every 400 operations outside the timed region to keep the history short, except in the history full scenario.",
        "A transaction computes its patch when it commits, so its synchronous and total overhead are the same work.",
        "Median hides the occasional pause. The mean and the 90th percentile of the pairs are in the result file."
      ],
